WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.842
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:07.112 --> 00:09.031
[theme music playing]

3
00:46.694 --> 00:50.030
A LOVE OTHER THAN YOURS

4
00:50.155 --> 00:51.407
[theme music concludes]

5
00:52.616 --> 00:53.450
ALL PERSONS, LOCATIONS, RELIGIONS, INCIDENTS, AND ORGANIZATIONS IN THIS DRAMA

6
00:53.576 --> 00:54.410
ARE FICTITIOUS

7
00:54.535 --> 00:55.369
CHILD ACTORS HAVE FILMED SAFELY UNDER PARENTAL SUPERVISION

8
00:55.494 --> 00:56.328
SCENES INVOLVING ANIMALS WERE FILMED SAFELY WITH EXPERT ADVICE AND COOPERATION

9
00:57.162 --> 00:58.289
[tense music playing]

10
00:58.414 --> 01:00.499
JAEKANG LAW FIRM

11
01:01.500 --> 01:02.626
[pants]

12
01:02.751 --> 01:04.003
Tell me where Mr. Seo is.

13
01:04.128 --> 01:07.256
[assistant] He's on his way to the airport for his New York trip.

14
01:13.554 --> 01:16.265
[phone vibrating]

15
01:20.936 --> 01:23.522
This little prank of yours has gone too far, Mr. Seo.

16
01:24.815 --> 01:27.401
-Sir, Lee Mi-do… -[Ju-hyeok] "November 3rd, 2010."

17
01:28.152 --> 01:32.031
"I will end his life in the most brutal way possible."

18
01:33.532 --> 01:35.284
"How do you think I should kill him?"

19
01:36.368 --> 01:38.329
"No one can know it was me, though."

20
01:39.371 --> 01:40.706
"That's very important."

21
01:41.540 --> 01:42.791
"I'll start a fire."

22
01:42.917 --> 01:45.502
"I'll make it look like there was a short circuit."

23
01:46.795 --> 01:49.048
"Something very similar happened recently."

24
01:50.299 --> 01:54.970
"So no one will think that I started the fire on purpose."

25
01:55.095 --> 01:56.430
[music rises]

26
01:57.431 --> 01:58.849
[Ju-hyeok] But I am certainly curious.

27
01:59.767 --> 02:02.186
Where would you be now if it weren't for me?

28
02:03.771 --> 02:05.230
I'll close the case for you,

29
02:05.356 --> 02:08.859
but send me all your files by the end of the day.

30
02:10.694 --> 02:12.154
It's been 16 years.

31
02:14.198 --> 02:18.118
Wouldn't it be upsetting if things ended on a sad note?

32
02:19.703 --> 02:21.246
[exhales shakily]

33
02:32.925 --> 02:34.885
-[tense music concludes] -[Tae-seung retching]

34
02:40.933 --> 02:42.017
[toilet flushes]

35
02:42.142 --> 02:44.561
[panting]

36
02:53.112 --> 02:54.989
[delicate string music playing]

37
03:00.536 --> 03:02.121
[dog barking]

38
03:02.830 --> 03:03.664
Hello.

39
03:04.623 --> 03:08.919
Listen, I'm here to give you that opportunity right now.

40
03:09.420 --> 03:12.089
Your Honor, please, give my client the chance

41
03:12.214 --> 03:13.590
to move forward with his life.

42
03:13.924 --> 03:15.092
Defendant Han Tae-seung,

43
03:15.217 --> 03:17.136
on the charge of committing arson resulting in a fatality…

44
03:17.261 --> 03:18.262
DEFENSE, DEFENDANT

45
03:18.387 --> 03:20.514
…the court finds you not guilty.

46
03:20.639 --> 03:22.599
-You're free to go now. -[gavel bangs]

47
03:23.434 --> 03:24.435
[slurps]

48
03:25.602 --> 03:26.520
Ah!

49
03:29.773 --> 03:31.316
What about my bag?

50
03:34.236 --> 03:35.320
You couldn't find it?

51
03:36.780 --> 03:37.614
No.

52
03:38.782 --> 03:41.410
Hey, how do you expect me to find it, huh?

53
03:41.994 --> 03:45.622
I may be a very good lawyer, but I'm not a detective.

54
03:45.873 --> 03:46.707
Why?

55
03:47.916 --> 03:49.501
Was something important in it?

56
03:49.626 --> 03:50.836
Want me to look again?

57
03:51.670 --> 03:53.338
No, it's fine.

58
03:55.007 --> 03:56.133
Don't look for it.

59
03:59.595 --> 04:00.429
Okay.

60
04:03.515 --> 04:04.683
[slurps]

61
04:28.540 --> 04:29.708
[delicate string music concludes]

62
04:30.459 --> 04:31.543
Hey, Wan-do.

63
04:34.379 --> 04:35.380
Yeah, she's sleeping.

64
04:38.008 --> 04:40.385
Tell Ms. Ma that she shouldn't worry too much.

65
04:43.889 --> 04:45.099
Go to sleep, yeah?

66
04:47.518 --> 04:48.519
[grunts softly]

67
05:07.830 --> 05:09.289
[tender music playing]

68
05:21.760 --> 05:23.053
[exhales sharply]

69
05:44.158 --> 05:45.492
BROTHER CLEANING

70
05:45.617 --> 05:46.660
[tender music concludes]

71
05:47.744 --> 05:48.704
[Wan-do] Hold on!

72
05:52.332 --> 05:54.042
[Mi-do] Oh, jeez. Thank you.

73
05:54.168 --> 05:55.002
[Wan-do] Sure.

74
05:56.545 --> 05:57.838
-Go. -[Wan-do] Sure.

75
05:59.381 --> 06:00.966
-See ya. -Just go away.

76
06:01.091 --> 06:03.427
["Striped Sweater" playing]

77
06:11.101 --> 06:12.144
YUSEONG UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

78
06:12.269 --> 06:13.103
Namgung.

79
06:13.812 --> 06:14.730
How was it?

80
06:14.855 --> 06:15.689
[grunts] Hungry?

81
06:15.814 --> 06:16.732
Starving.

82
06:16.857 --> 06:18.108
-Let's go eat. -Okay.

83
06:21.695 --> 06:24.239
[physical therapist] That's it. Just a little more.

84
06:24.364 --> 06:25.616
That's really good.

85
06:28.202 --> 06:29.286
That's it.

86
06:29.411 --> 06:30.412
You're doing great, honey.

87
06:30.537 --> 06:31.371
Very good.

88
06:32.331 --> 06:33.582
[Mi-do] That looks really warm.

89
06:34.791 --> 06:36.877
-[Namgung] I bought it on the street. -Really?

90
06:37.544 --> 06:38.462
Good for you.

91
06:38.587 --> 06:40.005
The Lunar New Year's soon.

92
06:40.631 --> 06:42.841
-Should I buy Ms. Ma a jacket? -She has many jackets.

93
06:42.966 --> 06:44.885
Her clothes had holes that she's sewn up and stuff.

94
06:45.010 --> 06:46.428
Yeah, but winter will end soon.

95
06:46.553 --> 06:48.305
-It's the New Year. -[laughs] Some daughter you are.

96
06:48.430 --> 06:49.640
Let's go shopping.

97
06:50.224 --> 06:53.143
3 MONTHS LATER

98
07:14.248 --> 07:16.083
Keep your elbows close, all right?

99
07:16.500 --> 07:18.085
That's right. Relax your shoulders.

100
07:18.210 --> 07:19.211
[exhales deeply]

101
07:19.336 --> 07:20.170
That's good.

102
07:21.421 --> 07:22.881
Today's your last session, honey.

103
07:23.507 --> 07:24.383
Hmm.

104
07:25.008 --> 07:28.136
These months went by slowly… [exhales] …and now they're done.

105
07:28.679 --> 07:30.430
And you've worked really hard.

106
07:30.555 --> 07:33.058
Oh, is your boyfriend picking you up again today?

107
07:35.269 --> 07:36.228
[chuckles softly]

108
07:37.354 --> 07:38.897
Thank you for what you do.

109
07:39.856 --> 07:41.608
Please give these to the other staff.

110
07:41.733 --> 07:43.777
[nurses chatting indistinctly]

111
07:45.153 --> 07:46.029
This is amazing.

112
07:47.030 --> 07:48.115
[chuckles softly]

113
07:50.117 --> 07:51.451
[song concludes]

114
07:51.576 --> 07:53.245
[chill instrumental music playing over speakers]

115
07:53.370 --> 07:55.497
Seems like work's been busy lately.

116
07:55.998 --> 07:58.083
It was busy because of month end, but it's fine.

117
07:58.542 --> 07:59.584
Hmm.

118
08:01.044 --> 08:04.214
Looks like you've been at the farms more than the lab lately.

119
08:05.507 --> 08:07.217
It's farm management season.

120
08:10.512 --> 08:12.014
Mm… Hmm.

121
08:17.936 --> 08:18.937
Mi-do.

122
08:19.062 --> 08:20.022
Hmm?

123
08:21.690 --> 08:22.691
We need to talk.

124
08:29.156 --> 08:31.283
[mariachi band playing "Bésame Mucho"]

125
08:38.248 --> 08:40.042
SEÑORITA, MARRY ME

126
08:43.670 --> 08:45.213
Oh, it's not her. It's not her.

127
08:45.339 --> 08:46.965
-She's over here. -[band stops playing]

128
08:48.800 --> 08:50.510
[patrons mumbling]

129
08:51.386 --> 08:52.220
Sorry, sir.

130
08:53.638 --> 08:55.223
[mariachi band playing "Bésame Mucho"]

131
09:08.028 --> 09:09.237
[band stops playing]

132
09:09.363 --> 09:10.447
[man] Thank you so much.

133
09:10.989 --> 09:13.200
-Thank you. Thank you. -Thank you. Thank you.

134
09:14.368 --> 09:15.452
Gosh!

135
09:22.417 --> 09:23.502
[clears throat]

136
09:24.628 --> 09:25.754
[exhales deeply]

137
09:27.547 --> 09:29.758
"Bésame Mucho," why did he choose it? It's terrible.

138
09:30.509 --> 09:32.219
That's right. [laughs lightly]

139
09:34.012 --> 09:34.930
Mmm.

140
09:35.430 --> 09:36.473
So you were saying something?

141
09:46.691 --> 09:48.527
What I said before still stands.

142
09:51.196 --> 09:52.239
What do you mean?

143
09:52.823 --> 09:54.491
It's fine if you want to go see him.

144
09:56.952 --> 09:58.662
You were busy with your treatment before.

145
09:58.787 --> 09:59.621
[soft music playing]

146
10:00.372 --> 10:01.623
Now that you're okay…

147
10:04.459 --> 10:06.086
you can think about it, Mi-do.

148
10:07.838 --> 10:08.964
[sighs softly]

149
10:09.297 --> 10:11.216
Think only of yourself, not me.

150
10:12.717 --> 10:14.302
I can always wait.

151
10:21.059 --> 10:22.436
[sighs]

152
10:34.823 --> 10:36.783
[inhales] Stop the car, please.

153
10:37.951 --> 10:38.952
We need to talk.

154
10:51.089 --> 10:52.048
[soft music concludes]

155
10:52.632 --> 10:54.009
Are you being serious, Namgung?

156
10:55.552 --> 10:56.928
Would you be fine with that?

157
10:57.262 --> 10:58.972
You said you had felt a spark.

158
11:00.307 --> 11:02.225
You said he flipped a switch inside you.

159
11:03.894 --> 11:05.145
So it's fine if you do it.

160
11:06.188 --> 11:07.981
Namgung, what are you talking about?

161
11:08.398 --> 11:09.816
Why do you say it so casually?

162
11:10.567 --> 11:11.693
It's like you're recommending a coach.

163
11:11.818 --> 11:14.112
Plus, are you insane or what?

164
11:14.362 --> 11:15.864
We're getting married anyway.

165
11:17.866 --> 11:19.367
You and I are going to be together.

166
11:20.410 --> 11:22.287
Yet you're spouting this crazy talk?

167
11:23.288 --> 11:24.122
Hey, Namgung!

168
11:24.247 --> 11:27.792
Instead of marrying me full of regrets, you should see him.

169
11:28.251 --> 11:30.795
That way you will finally sort your feelings out, Mi-do.

170
11:42.390 --> 11:44.309
So I can sleep with him then?

171
11:46.019 --> 11:49.397
What? I can't? You told me to see him.

172
11:50.482 --> 11:53.026
I need to find out how compatible we really are.

173
11:53.902 --> 11:56.863
That way, I'll move on without any regrets. Agree?

174
11:57.572 --> 11:59.282
If you want to, then do it.

175
12:01.493 --> 12:02.911
Then I can go all the way, huh?

176
12:03.787 --> 12:05.038
You know what I like.

177
12:05.163 --> 12:06.831
-[cheeky music playing] -***'s my thing,

178
12:06.957 --> 12:10.210
and *** makes me really turned on. Hmm?

179
12:10.919 --> 12:12.921
Is it okay? Hmm?

180
12:13.046 --> 12:14.172
Lick his ***, please.

181
12:15.507 --> 12:17.842
Oh, and ***jobs are your favorite.

182
12:18.385 --> 12:20.303
*** *** *** ***, okay, do it!

183
12:20.428 --> 12:21.805
Right! I'll do it all!

184
12:21.930 --> 12:23.306
I'll do whatever I want!

185
12:23.431 --> 12:26.184
*** a*** and jerk ***, and I will do it all!

186
12:26.309 --> 12:27.435
Yeah, do it all!

187
12:27.894 --> 12:28.979
Jeez!

188
12:30.522 --> 12:31.856
[passers-by whispering indistinctly]

189
12:31.982 --> 12:33.817
[woman] Oh, my God. Did you see that?

190
12:33.942 --> 12:36.653
-[cheeky music concludes] -[crow cawing]

191
12:36.778 --> 12:38.321
[frumpy jazz music playing]

192
12:45.620 --> 12:46.538
[groans]

193
12:46.663 --> 12:47.789
Shit.

194
12:53.003 --> 12:54.379
[exhales deeply]

195
12:56.006 --> 12:57.340
[frumpy jazz music concludes]

196
12:57.465 --> 12:59.759
I didn't suggest this to start a fight with you here.

197
13:01.928 --> 13:03.680
I didn't say it out of anger.

198
13:05.265 --> 13:07.058
I thought about it for a long time.

199
13:19.195 --> 13:20.155
Namgung.

200
13:22.157 --> 13:24.618
You really don't mind if I go out with other guys?

201
13:27.579 --> 13:28.413
Yeah.

202
13:29.039 --> 13:30.415
As long as you're happy.

203
13:36.463 --> 13:37.380
Hmm.

204
13:38.965 --> 13:40.175
Then you do it too.

205
13:42.719 --> 13:43.887
Go out with other women.

206
13:44.471 --> 13:45.388
That's fair, Namgung.

207
13:46.640 --> 13:48.266
-Hey, Mi-do… -You do it.

208
13:51.436 --> 13:53.229
I'm not doing it until you do it.

209
13:56.900 --> 13:58.109
[sighs]

210
13:58.234 --> 14:00.028
[gentle, emotional music playing]

211
14:04.491 --> 14:08.620
A LOVE OTHER THAN YOURS

212
14:08.745 --> 14:14.626
WHAT REMAINS OF OUR PASSIONATE LOVE?

213
14:22.425 --> 14:24.052
[Su-a] Stay here until the cast is off.

214
14:25.553 --> 14:27.013
Work will keep me late.

215
14:28.682 --> 14:29.599
Hey.

216
14:31.142 --> 14:33.269
Are you still really mad at me?

217
14:36.731 --> 14:37.649
[vending machine thuds]

218
14:38.316 --> 14:39.317
[sighs]

219
14:40.151 --> 14:42.612
[young Su-a panting]

220
14:42.737 --> 14:44.906
I couldn't call because I was in Himado.

221
14:47.200 --> 14:49.369
-So my dad… -I didn't make the debut lineup.

222
14:56.167 --> 14:57.544
I left the dorm too.

223
14:58.128 --> 14:59.170
I can't be an idol.

224
15:01.339 --> 15:02.590
I was shocked by the news.

225
15:02.716 --> 15:04.050
I messed up on stage.

226
15:05.468 --> 15:08.638
Oh, and I heard that our fathers broke up.

227
15:10.682 --> 15:12.434
They know I tipped off the press.

228
15:14.561 --> 15:15.603
I'm sorry.

229
15:18.106 --> 15:19.399
Are you really sorry?

230
15:20.442 --> 15:21.818
Then you should quit.

231
15:22.777 --> 15:23.695
You give up.

232
15:24.821 --> 15:25.989
Give up on your dream.

233
15:33.288 --> 15:36.458
[Su-yeon] I said it out of anger. I didn't want you to fail at all.

234
15:37.917 --> 15:43.381
I just… I want us to go back to how we used to be.

235
15:44.007 --> 15:45.383
That's why I came here.

236
15:46.176 --> 15:49.929
Because… I want us to be friends again.

237
15:56.728 --> 15:58.146
Then get it together.

238
16:00.148 --> 16:02.734
Stop dating jerks and showing up like this here.

239
16:04.944 --> 16:06.112
Get your act together.

240
16:13.745 --> 16:14.704
[Su-yeon] Su-a?

241
16:19.167 --> 16:20.919
You're as selfish as ever.

242
16:33.973 --> 16:37.018
[footsteps receding]

243
16:37.143 --> 16:38.353
-[scoffs softly] -[door closes]

244
16:38.478 --> 16:40.104
[gentle, emotional music concludes]

245
17:01.960 --> 17:03.044
[Dong-hwan] He's relentless.

246
17:03.169 --> 17:04.087
NAMGUNG HO, OUT OF OFFICE

247
17:04.671 --> 17:06.548
[Dong-hwan] He was fine in the anchovy boat.

248
17:07.632 --> 17:09.217
He even hung out in the pig farm.

249
17:09.843 --> 17:11.678
[sighs] He's very relentless.

250
17:13.263 --> 17:15.890
You should have sent him just straight to the worst factory.

251
17:16.015 --> 17:17.225
[groans]

252
17:17.350 --> 17:19.185
And the money Food Hobbit gave him.

253
17:19.310 --> 17:20.645
Who knew it was a crash settlement?

254
17:20.770 --> 17:21.938
[sighs]

255
17:22.063 --> 17:23.356
Besides, he even pays

256
17:23.481 --> 17:25.692
the partner company's coffee bills electronically.

257
17:25.817 --> 17:27.735
We won't find anything even if we dig.

258
17:28.236 --> 17:30.363
Yeah, but we can't keep him here forever.

259
17:30.488 --> 17:31.573
[groans]

260
17:31.948 --> 17:32.782
Come on.

261
17:33.199 --> 17:34.158
You always worry.

262
17:34.284 --> 17:35.410
Always, always.

263
17:35.535 --> 17:36.411
Stop worrying.

264
17:36.911 --> 17:39.038
I'm the youngest manager here. Huh?

265
17:39.539 --> 17:42.959
I wanted to see how much he knows, and I was just testing him, okay?

266
17:43.960 --> 17:45.253
I'll deal with him soon.

267
17:45.962 --> 17:48.339
So all you have to do is sit back and decide.

268
17:48.840 --> 17:51.426
Whether to send him to the Wonju Plant or the Taean Plant, sir.

269
17:51.551 --> 17:53.469
What do you think? Hmm?

270
17:53.928 --> 17:54.846
[Namgung] The Busan Plant.

271
17:56.014 --> 17:56.931
Oh, what the…

272
17:57.557 --> 17:59.267
[bold music playing]

273
18:02.395 --> 18:03.855
AMSEONG MUGWORT FARM CONTRACT

274
18:05.690 --> 18:07.025
I love the wheat noodles there.

275
18:07.150 --> 18:08.276
Oh!

276
18:12.071 --> 18:13.364
OUT OF OFFICE

277
18:14.699 --> 18:15.783
Oh, shit.

278
18:17.869 --> 18:18.953
[bold music concludes]

279
18:19.579 --> 18:22.457
[phone vibrating]

280
18:29.422 --> 18:30.965
[phone continues vibrating]

281
18:31.841 --> 18:32.842
What is this?

282
18:32.967 --> 18:33.801
Huh?

283
18:34.802 --> 18:36.429
Why are you ignoring my calls?

284
18:37.055 --> 18:39.849
I called you so many times for that price report.

285
18:39.974 --> 18:41.893
PURCHASING ASSISTANT MANAGER NAMGUNG HO

286
18:42.060 --> 18:43.603
ASSHOLE MANAGER JEONG YEON-HO

287
18:44.020 --> 18:45.688
Is this how my name is saved?

288
18:45.813 --> 18:47.148
[upbeat, confident music playing]

289
18:47.273 --> 18:50.193
[phone continues vibrating]

290
18:51.527 --> 18:52.612
Namgung…

291
18:54.572 --> 18:56.115
How do you have me saved in your phone?

292
18:56.240 --> 18:57.659
Asshole Manager Jeong.

293
18:58.618 --> 18:59.494
Pardon me?

294
18:59.619 --> 19:01.496
I almost saved you as "*** Asshole,"

295
19:02.288 --> 19:03.665
but I just went with "Asshole."

296
19:04.165 --> 19:04.999
Why?

297
19:06.209 --> 19:07.126
Should I change it?

298
19:07.251 --> 19:08.252
No, not really.

299
19:09.837 --> 19:10.922
This is insubordination.

300
19:12.048 --> 19:14.050
I understand that I'm new, but I'm still your boss.

301
19:14.175 --> 19:16.761
You can't do this. You think I'll stand here and-- Oh!

302
19:20.348 --> 19:21.224
[stammers]

303
19:21.766 --> 19:22.850
What?

304
19:31.651 --> 19:32.485
Hey.

305
19:33.820 --> 19:34.654
Huh?

306
19:35.321 --> 19:36.614
Let me ask you something.

307
19:40.952 --> 19:44.664
Why do you think we track the prices of imported materials?

308
19:45.915 --> 19:52.171
Well, that's to see the price trends from all of our suppliers.

309
19:53.256 --> 19:54.590
It's for cost management.

310
19:55.591 --> 19:57.427
And to stay on budget, yeah.

311
19:57.552 --> 19:58.636
Hmm.

312
19:59.846 --> 20:00.680
No.

313
20:02.098 --> 20:05.893
We track price changes for us to check the cost structure.

314
20:06.853 --> 20:10.523
That's why instead of shipping records, we check the raw material prices

315
20:10.648 --> 20:12.316
and exchange rates in the last three years.

316
20:12.442 --> 20:13.276
We do it diligently.

317
20:14.193 --> 20:15.903
Well, of course, there's also that too.

318
20:16.446 --> 20:17.488
[inhales deeply]

319
20:17.613 --> 20:20.491
Whether you bully me or run me ragged, I don't care about that.

320
20:20.616 --> 20:21.451
But listen…

321
20:24.370 --> 20:25.913
your sheer incompetence,

322
20:28.041 --> 20:31.461
don't you dare show it right in front of me ever.

323
20:32.754 --> 20:33.838
It pisses me off.

324
20:39.719 --> 20:41.095
Oh, shit.

325
20:41.721 --> 20:43.181
[upbeat, confident music concludes]

326
20:44.432 --> 20:45.308
Go on.

327
20:46.601 --> 20:47.643
Get out.

328
20:47.977 --> 20:49.145
[stammers]

329
21:06.245 --> 21:08.122
[soft, pensive music playing]

330
21:09.832 --> 21:10.875
[Mi-do] Go out with other women.

331
21:11.375 --> 21:12.293
That's fair, Namgung.

332
21:13.252 --> 21:15.088
-Hey, Mi-do… -You do it.

333
21:17.173 --> 21:19.217
I'm not doing it until you do it.

334
21:23.596 --> 21:24.722
One week.

335
21:27.100 --> 21:28.309
I'll give you one week.

336
21:29.644 --> 21:30.937
Think about it seriously.

337
21:32.230 --> 21:33.606
[soft, pensive music concludes]

338
21:36.859 --> 21:38.569
[seabirds calling]

339
21:41.906 --> 21:43.533
[Yeon-ho] Go get some mudflat samples.

340
21:44.283 --> 21:45.910
The salinity varies a lot from high tide,

341
21:46.035 --> 21:48.246
so take samples every 164 feet

342
21:48.371 --> 21:49.831
and dig down at least four inches.

343
21:51.707 --> 21:52.917
Have fun with that.

344
21:53.835 --> 21:55.628
[weary blues music playing]

345
21:58.631 --> 21:59.549
[sighs]

346
22:07.640 --> 22:08.724
[shovel scraping]

347
22:11.561 --> 22:13.020
Sir, can I ask you something?

348
22:13.771 --> 22:15.857
I'm here to collect mudflat samples, sir.

349
22:16.524 --> 22:17.483
Do I go that way?

350
22:17.608 --> 22:20.570
Uh, you just need to head straight in over there.

351
22:21.028 --> 22:23.656
But listen, the terrain there, it is pretty unusual.

352
22:24.031 --> 22:25.366
The tide comes in real fast.

353
22:25.783 --> 22:26.617
So be careful, huh?

354
22:27.451 --> 22:28.578
Thank you very much.

355
22:31.622 --> 22:33.040
[shovel scraping]

356
22:33.166 --> 22:34.417
[weary blues music concludes]

357
22:35.668 --> 22:36.711
Wait a second.

358
22:37.378 --> 22:39.672
It's a spring tide today, so the water will rise.

359
22:40.298 --> 22:41.549
I hope you'll be all right.

360
22:42.633 --> 22:44.468
[jaunty music playing]

361
22:49.473 --> 22:50.391
[grunts]

362
23:03.237 --> 23:04.280
[sighs]

363
23:10.411 --> 23:11.621
[mud crunches]

364
23:12.288 --> 23:13.247
[mud squelches]

365
23:13.372 --> 23:14.582
Whoa!

366
23:14.707 --> 23:15.875
[music rises]

367
23:35.853 --> 23:38.272
Should I join the union and claim hazard pay?

368
23:44.403 --> 23:45.655
[jaunty music concludes]

369
23:47.657 --> 23:48.491
[grunts]

370
23:54.205 --> 23:55.289
Sh…

371
24:00.419 --> 24:01.629
[sighs]

372
24:02.964 --> 24:04.340
[sighs deeply]

373
24:05.007 --> 24:06.592
[seabirds calling]

374
24:06.717 --> 24:08.511
[foreboding music playing]

375
24:15.393 --> 24:17.353
[village head] You just need to head straight in over there.

376
24:17.478 --> 24:20.398
But listen, the terrain there, it is pretty unusual.

377
24:20.523 --> 24:23.526
The tide comes in real fast, so be careful.

378
24:54.307 --> 24:55.599
[foreboding music concludes]

379
24:55.850 --> 24:58.060
[urgent music playing]

380
25:04.233 --> 25:07.528
[panting]

381
25:18.039 --> 25:18.998
[gasps]

382
25:19.707 --> 25:20.958
I'm sorry, ma'am. Sorry, ma'am.

383
25:21.083 --> 25:25.171
EXPRESS BUS TERMINAL

384
25:27.298 --> 25:28.799
[music softens]

385
25:43.022 --> 25:43.939
[urgent music concludes]

386
25:44.565 --> 25:45.858
I think we've met before.

387
25:48.069 --> 25:49.236
TF TEAM 3, PARK SU-A

388
25:50.529 --> 25:53.407
I'm Park Su-a from TF Team 3.

389
26:00.581 --> 26:02.375
As I mentioned on the phone,

390
26:03.459 --> 26:05.628
Mr. Namgung was collecting salinity samples

391
26:05.878 --> 26:07.963
when the tide quickly rushed in.

392
26:09.131 --> 26:11.133
The accident was promptly reported

393
26:12.385 --> 26:14.387
at 11:23 a.m. on the dot.

394
26:15.054 --> 26:16.597
The search began at 12:00 p.m.

395
26:17.556 --> 26:20.976
Currently two coastal rescue boats and two search drones are deployed,

396
26:21.560 --> 26:23.521
searching a three-mile radius.

397
26:25.106 --> 26:28.526
The purchasing department is currently in a meeting with the director,

398
26:28.651 --> 26:30.194
so I was sent to assess the situation.

399
26:31.737 --> 26:33.739
Once the company forms a response team,

400
26:34.740 --> 26:36.951
the executives will come down, even at dawn.

401
26:37.201 --> 26:39.787
-They will come to oversee-- -They should be doing more than that.

402
26:42.123 --> 26:43.958
Why are they looking in a three-mile radius?

403
26:44.792 --> 26:47.628
That boy who went missing just last month in Sokcho

404
26:47.753 --> 26:50.548
was found 12 miles away in less than three hours.

405
26:51.298 --> 26:53.217
As you said, that was a child,

406
26:53.342 --> 26:55.261
so the search priorities were different.

407
26:56.262 --> 26:57.430
Our priorities--

408
26:57.555 --> 27:00.015
Stop saying that they won't look for him just because he's an adult.

409
27:02.059 --> 27:03.936
Hunmin Confectionery won't do anything.

410
27:04.437 --> 27:06.063
Isn't that why it's dragging?

411
27:07.398 --> 27:08.649
You gotta call someone.

412
27:09.567 --> 27:12.528
Either your boss or someone who makes at least three times what you do.

413
27:13.279 --> 27:14.780
Tell them I'm a crazy bitch.

414
27:15.531 --> 27:17.575
Tell them I'll go to the press in 30 minutes.

415
27:19.201 --> 27:20.619
I'm sure that won't work.

416
27:25.040 --> 27:26.584
I confronted them earlier.

417
27:39.305 --> 27:41.515
He makes five times more than I do.

418
27:41.640 --> 27:44.268
YOON DO-HAK EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR, PRODUCTION

419
27:46.645 --> 27:48.230
It doesn't matter if I complain.

420
27:48.355 --> 27:49.607
If you do it, it might work.

421
27:50.691 --> 27:51.901
So call him yourself.

422
27:53.068 --> 27:54.445
Tell him that you're crazy.

423
27:56.447 --> 27:58.157
And that you'll go to the press in ten.

424
27:59.950 --> 28:01.285
[tender, hopeful music playing]

425
28:01.410 --> 28:03.120
[Su-a] Tell him I gave you his card.

426
28:12.713 --> 28:14.006
[exhales deeply]

427
28:16.050 --> 28:18.052
[motorboat engine whirring]

428
28:25.893 --> 28:26.852
[dialing]

429
28:26.977 --> 28:28.854
-[radio static buzzes] -[rescue worker] This is Rescue.

430
28:28.979 --> 28:31.565
Missing person found at the reef west of Sector 7.

431
28:43.786 --> 28:45.329
[gurney rattling]

432
28:49.041 --> 28:50.918
Father!

433
28:52.169 --> 28:53.546
Father!

434
28:54.380 --> 28:55.881
Daddy!

435
28:56.507 --> 28:57.883
Daddy!

436
28:58.926 --> 29:01.220
Daddy!

437
29:04.473 --> 29:07.434
[indistinct crowd chatter]

438
29:09.353 --> 29:10.938
[tender, hopeful music concludes]

439
29:12.523 --> 29:14.108
[gentle music playing]

440
29:16.485 --> 29:17.736
Hey, Mi-do.

441
29:26.662 --> 29:27.663
Was it Ho-sik?

442
29:28.581 --> 29:29.748
Did Ho-sik tell you?

443
29:32.209 --> 29:34.211
Oh, my manager, that idiot.

444
29:46.557 --> 29:48.309
[breathes deeply]

445
29:55.441 --> 29:58.110
[sobbing softly]

446
29:58.235 --> 30:00.070
[Ho-sik] He's been missing for over an hour.

447
30:00.863 --> 30:02.865
The purchasing department is keeping quiet.

448
30:04.074 --> 30:05.618
I'll head down after my meeting.

449
30:06.201 --> 30:07.911
You go first, Ms. Park.

450
30:15.169 --> 30:17.713
-[gate opens] -[exhales deeply]

451
30:20.382 --> 30:22.384
[gentle music concludes]

452
30:44.406 --> 30:45.908
[gate closes]

453
30:53.040 --> 30:53.957
[Mi-do] Deok-sun?

454
30:54.083 --> 30:57.044
Mm-hmm. The Haemado Guesthouse owner's niece, Mi-do Lee.

455
30:57.294 --> 30:59.505
Don't gossip when you don't know anything about him.

456
31:00.631 --> 31:02.966
Focus on your own work instead of gossiping.

457
31:03.217 --> 31:04.885
I confronted them earlier.

458
31:28.617 --> 31:30.452
-[door opens] -[soft music playing]

459
31:36.875 --> 31:39.294
[Namgung] The thing is, I dated her for ten years.

460
31:40.003 --> 31:41.046
So I ran away.

461
31:41.171 --> 31:43.048
-[women] Ran away? -[Namgung] Yeah.

462
31:43.882 --> 31:45.467
It was too hard seeing her.

463
31:47.678 --> 31:48.595
[grunts softly]

464
31:51.265 --> 31:53.475
What's on your mind? You didn't even see me coming.

465
31:54.685 --> 31:57.563
It's just that I had a very long day today thanks to someone.

466
31:58.731 --> 31:59.773
Yeah, me as well.

467
32:06.363 --> 32:07.531
[sighs deeply]

468
32:12.995 --> 32:13.829
Oh.

469
32:17.583 --> 32:19.001
You could use one right now.

470
32:20.335 --> 32:21.211
[chuckles]

471
32:28.177 --> 32:29.178
You're still smoking?

472
32:30.345 --> 32:32.389
-Since all the way back then? -[Su-a] Yeah.

473
32:35.601 --> 32:37.603
-I go through a lot. -Hey!

474
32:37.728 --> 32:38.896
Are you mad…

475
32:40.898 --> 32:41.940
Are you crazy?

476
32:42.065 --> 32:42.900
Are you…

477
32:43.650 --> 32:45.235
You're way too young to be smoking.

478
32:45.360 --> 32:46.361
[scoffs]

479
32:47.029 --> 32:49.323
Twenty-eight isn't exactly way too young, I think.

480
32:50.365 --> 32:51.200
You're 28?

481
32:55.245 --> 32:56.246
You are that old?

482
33:05.964 --> 33:06.799
Okay.

483
33:08.008 --> 33:09.218
Thanks for everything.

484
33:11.220 --> 33:13.013
I heard you worked really hard today.

485
33:15.766 --> 33:16.809
It was nothing.

486
33:18.477 --> 33:20.437
And you looked after my girlfriend, too.

487
33:23.690 --> 33:25.067
I'll buy you lunch sometime.

488
33:26.276 --> 33:27.486
Get some rest.

489
33:27.611 --> 33:28.862
[gentle music concludes]

490
33:32.324 --> 33:33.534
Please never do that again.

491
33:38.664 --> 33:41.208
I was so scared I'd never see you again.

492
33:43.293 --> 33:45.879
I was really worried about you, so don't…

493
33:48.590 --> 33:50.509
Never do something so dangerous again.

494
33:52.553 --> 33:54.304
-Never. -Stop there, please.

495
33:57.391 --> 33:59.351
Or I won't be buying you lunch.

496
34:03.313 --> 34:04.147
Rest.

497
34:08.277 --> 34:09.778
[tender music playing]

498
34:19.204 --> 34:20.205
You're still awake.

499
34:20.330 --> 34:23.458
[Mi-do grunts softly] Where did you go?

500
34:23.959 --> 34:24.960
To get some air.

501
34:25.085 --> 34:27.004
I didn't get to thank Su-a earlier.

502
34:30.215 --> 34:31.174
That's her, right?

503
34:32.092 --> 34:33.427
Deok-sun from Haemado.

504
34:33.969 --> 34:35.429
The one you saw again at work.

505
34:35.888 --> 34:37.097
Mm-hmm, that's her.

506
34:37.556 --> 34:38.724
She looks the same.

507
34:41.810 --> 34:42.644
So true.

508
34:49.359 --> 34:50.193
Sorry.

509
34:52.404 --> 34:53.989
What are you sorry for?

510
34:54.448 --> 34:56.783
You must have been scared by the call.

511
35:00.495 --> 35:01.872
You despise the ocean.

512
35:04.374 --> 35:06.501
Who else was gonna come for you?

513
35:07.711 --> 35:09.087
Lee Yeong-do, that half-wit?

514
35:09.838 --> 35:11.089
Lee Wan-do, that idiot?

515
35:11.214 --> 35:12.382
[chuckles]

516
35:13.300 --> 35:15.636
Aren't you roasting your own brothers, honey?

517
35:21.141 --> 35:22.517
Let's get some sleep.

518
35:22.643 --> 35:24.394
We have to head up early tomorrow.

519
35:28.023 --> 35:29.650
[exhales deeply]

520
35:31.735 --> 35:32.861
[whispers] Okay.

521
35:40.786 --> 35:41.995
[tender music concludes]

522
35:54.341 --> 35:55.717
Call me when you get there.

523
36:00.931 --> 36:01.974
Mi-do.

524
36:03.308 --> 36:05.477
I hate it too, but what choice do I have?

525
36:06.228 --> 36:09.356
The big boss paying my salary told me to finish up here.

526
36:10.023 --> 36:11.733
I could stay here with you and then go.

527
36:11.858 --> 36:12.818
It's all right.

528
36:14.987 --> 36:16.405
You should get back to the city.

529
36:18.532 --> 36:21.118
I know you hate the ocean, and I can't see you stressed.

530
36:24.955 --> 36:27.666
Su-a, is she staying with you?

531
36:29.209 --> 36:30.168
Yeah, they told her to.

532
36:31.169 --> 36:32.004
You know, right?

533
36:34.631 --> 36:35.882
You know that she has…

534
36:36.508 --> 36:38.343
Park Su-a has feelings for you.

535
36:40.345 --> 36:41.805
[soft music playing]

536
36:45.976 --> 36:47.102
[inhales deeply]

537
36:47.894 --> 36:49.813
I haven't done anything wrong, Mi-do.

538
36:50.689 --> 36:53.775
And as for her, she's just some kid I knew.

539
36:54.568 --> 36:56.820
And now she's just another office worker.

540
36:58.196 --> 36:59.906
And I've never given her signals.

541
37:00.657 --> 37:01.867
You have one day left.

542
37:06.329 --> 37:08.457
I said you should go out with other women.

543
37:10.709 --> 37:12.002
You agreed to think about it.

544
37:13.545 --> 37:14.755
You have one day left.

545
37:16.298 --> 37:17.382
[sighs]

546
37:20.927 --> 37:22.721
The bus is leaving. Get on.

547
37:32.939 --> 37:34.399
-Where's Mr. Namgung? -[woman] Huh?

548
37:34.983 --> 37:37.986
Oh, he left for the mudflats ages ago.

549
37:38.570 --> 37:41.198
He took his girlfriend to the bus bright and early.

550
37:41.698 --> 37:45.368
He's the early bird. [laughs]

551
37:46.286 --> 37:47.287
God damn it.

552
37:47.412 --> 37:51.083
[panting]

553
38:17.526 --> 38:18.443
[Mi-do grunts]

554
38:20.028 --> 38:21.863
Hey, why are you here?

555
38:21.988 --> 38:23.740
You didn't send me off out of worry.

556
38:24.783 --> 38:25.992
It's because I'm a pain.

557
38:27.244 --> 38:28.829
Where is this coming from, huh?

558
38:36.086 --> 38:37.129
Is it about Su-a?

559
38:40.298 --> 38:41.216
We talked about this.

560
38:41.341 --> 38:42.717
-Su-a is just-- -[Mi-do] I know.

561
38:43.468 --> 38:44.803
Su-a means nothing to you.

562
38:45.345 --> 38:46.680
This is not about her.

563
38:50.142 --> 38:50.976
Purchasing.

564
38:52.227 --> 38:53.812
You decided to change departments.

565
38:55.355 --> 38:56.773
Why didn't you tell me?

566
38:57.149 --> 38:59.568
Why? To avoid worrying me?

567
39:00.318 --> 39:01.444
[inhales deeply]

568
39:01.903 --> 39:02.863
I'm sorry.

569
39:04.906 --> 39:06.366
-I was going to tell you-- -No, Namgung.

570
39:06.491 --> 39:11.746
When you quit art, or when you were ruined because of Aunt Hwa-young,

571
39:13.039 --> 39:15.750
or when you gave away your entire lease deposit,

572
39:16.293 --> 39:18.795
or even when you gave your mom your stupid kidney,

573
39:19.421 --> 39:20.797
you never told me anything.

574
39:21.506 --> 39:24.176
And it was because you didn't want me to worry.

575
39:26.678 --> 39:28.930
I didn't want to be a burden, that's why.

576
39:31.850 --> 39:34.519
All those were my problems, so I had to handle them.

577
39:34.644 --> 39:35.478
But I know…

578
39:35.604 --> 39:36.688
[inhales deeply]

579
39:36.813 --> 39:38.315
I know that it hurt you.

580
39:41.943 --> 39:43.069
I'm sorry.

581
39:44.404 --> 39:45.363
It's all my fault.

582
39:46.239 --> 39:47.616
You're sorry, Namgung?

583
39:50.243 --> 39:51.328
No, you're not.

584
39:52.037 --> 39:53.413
I don't believe you're sorry.

585
39:56.041 --> 39:56.875
Namgung,

586
39:59.002 --> 40:01.421
I've known you since you were seven years old.

587
40:02.214 --> 40:03.840
I can read it in your eyes.

588
40:04.674 --> 40:08.803
I may not notice everything, but I notice when things are good for you,

589
40:08.929 --> 40:10.680
when they're bad for you, and besides…

590
40:12.849 --> 40:14.059
I know how you see me.

591
40:14.726 --> 40:16.102
I know what you think of me.

592
40:16.394 --> 40:17.437
I know it all.

593
40:20.315 --> 40:22.567
You think I am a despicable person.

594
40:22.692 --> 40:24.110
You hate me, and now I know it!

595
40:26.154 --> 40:27.781
Where is this coming from, huh?

596
40:28.365 --> 40:29.324
Shit.

597
40:32.744 --> 40:33.995
Mi-do!

598
40:35.413 --> 40:37.332
[panting]

599
40:40.293 --> 40:44.923
I don't know what has gotten into you, and I don't want to fight you.

600
40:45.465 --> 40:46.591
Go home now.

601
40:50.053 --> 40:51.012
What?

602
40:53.265 --> 40:55.433
You told me to go out with that man.

603
40:55.892 --> 40:57.894
Was it really just all for my own sake?

604
40:58.770 --> 40:59.771
No, it wasn't.

605
41:00.313 --> 41:02.065
You said it to hurt me, right?

606
41:03.608 --> 41:06.861
Sure, maybe 90% of it was for my sake.

607
41:06.987 --> 41:08.113
You probably meant it.

608
41:08.989 --> 41:10.657
But what about the other 10%?

609
41:11.116 --> 41:12.909
Was that 10% really for me?

610
41:13.910 --> 41:16.621
When you said that to me, didn't you think I would get hurt?

611
41:17.831 --> 41:18.873
Answer me!

612
41:18.999 --> 41:20.208
Answer me now!

613
41:25.672 --> 41:26.715
[exhales shakily]

614
41:28.300 --> 41:29.301
Yeah, Mi-do.

615
41:30.260 --> 41:31.428
I wanted you to suffer.

616
41:32.178 --> 41:33.013
Are you happy now?

617
41:35.682 --> 41:36.891
[Mi-do grunts]

618
41:38.018 --> 41:39.144
[despondent music playing]

619
41:39.269 --> 41:40.270
Why?

620
41:40.395 --> 41:41.938
[panting]

621
41:42.522 --> 41:43.606
I can't do that?

622
41:44.649 --> 41:47.736
Should I always be dragged around by you, afraid of getting dumped?

623
41:49.446 --> 41:52.866
I'm scared that I'd burden you, that I'd ruin your life.

624
41:52.991 --> 41:54.826
I know my life is shitty,

625
41:54.951 --> 41:57.287
and I always feel like I can barely breathe.

626
41:58.455 --> 42:00.540
But still, I lived on.

627
42:01.166 --> 42:03.043
I did it because of you.

628
42:04.461 --> 42:07.464
You're the reason I fought to survive.

629
42:08.089 --> 42:09.466
How could you do this to me?

630
42:09.591 --> 42:11.051
[sobbing]

631
42:12.469 --> 42:14.179
How could you say you liked another guy?

632
42:14.971 --> 42:17.640
That he flipped a switch on you and lit up your life. Why?

633
42:20.060 --> 42:23.355
Even when I asked, you should have denied and forgotten it.

634
42:24.439 --> 42:28.818
You should have sworn it wasn't true. Then I would've let it slide.

635
42:29.611 --> 42:32.113
I would've just turned a blind eye if you just let it go.

636
42:32.405 --> 42:34.532
Because I knew you would do that.

637
42:35.658 --> 42:37.535
But you shouldn't have to do it.

638
42:37.660 --> 42:41.373
I already feel so sorry for you, and I just ended up hurting you more.

639
42:41.915 --> 42:43.458
And I caused you more pain.

640
42:44.834 --> 42:47.420
Why don't you show me your pain? Huh?!

641
42:48.088 --> 42:49.798
I know I'm just a terrible bitch.

642
42:50.340 --> 42:51.966
Why are you holding it in?

643
42:53.176 --> 42:57.097
Namgung, you shouldn't hold in things like that.

644
42:57.347 --> 42:59.599
You're supposed to swear and get mad.

645
43:00.809 --> 43:02.602
[music rises]

646
43:03.978 --> 43:06.648
[Mi-do grunting]

647
43:11.945 --> 43:15.281
[sobbing]

648
43:19.244 --> 43:20.703
What do you want me to do?

649
43:21.413 --> 43:22.914
Once you're fixated on something,

650
43:23.039 --> 43:25.542
I know you won't let go, no matter what I say.

651
43:25.667 --> 43:26.918
Then what do you want me to do?

652
43:27.502 --> 43:29.003
What was I supposed to do, huh?

653
43:30.630 --> 43:33.091
You should have said we'd try together!

654
43:33.675 --> 43:35.802
Not to tell me to go see that guy, Namgung.

655
43:36.553 --> 43:39.806
Even if it's miserable for us both,

656
43:40.432 --> 43:42.434
you should have said we'd try anyway.

657
43:43.226 --> 43:44.060
[exhales deeply]

658
43:45.019 --> 43:46.813
But you didn't even want to try.

659
43:47.313 --> 43:48.982
You wanted to hurt me and that's it.

660
43:52.193 --> 43:54.362
Caring 90% and hurting me 10%.

661
43:55.488 --> 43:56.823
So sick and tired of it.

662
43:57.532 --> 44:01.369
Your pity and kindness, they're suffocating me too.

663
44:02.954 --> 44:05.165
If you want to hurt me, hurt me 100%

664
44:06.040 --> 44:09.669
If it comes from you, I'll gladly accept it.

665
44:10.628 --> 44:12.380
So give me 100%!

666
44:14.174 --> 44:17.469
[breathes deeply]

667
44:18.178 --> 44:20.847
[panting]

668
44:20.972 --> 44:22.390
[despondent music concludes]

669
44:27.270 --> 44:28.104
I'm back, ma'am.

670
44:28.229 --> 44:29.522
Oh? Wait…

671
44:30.148 --> 44:31.107
Back already?

672
44:34.944 --> 44:35.904
Oh?

673
44:37.322 --> 44:40.283
[seabirds calling]

674
44:47.373 --> 44:48.750
So when I'm back in Seoul,

675
44:50.835 --> 44:53.171
I'll ask him to date me for a whole month.

676
44:54.923 --> 44:56.591
You should date her as well.

677
45:05.558 --> 45:07.101
And besides, you were right.

678
45:15.818 --> 45:16.861
With you…

679
45:18.738 --> 45:20.740
I feel like I could go anywhere.

680
45:23.326 --> 45:24.577
Alone, I'm scared.

681
45:27.622 --> 45:28.790
And no matter where…

682
45:31.376 --> 45:33.002
I think I could go with you.

683
45:33.461 --> 45:35.755
[breathes deeply]

684
45:35.880 --> 45:37.632
[sentimental Korean pop song playing]

685
46:05.702 --> 46:09.122
[Mi-do] We deceive and lie to ourselves countless times during our lifetime.

686
46:10.707 --> 46:13.501
And we say that it's to protect the other person,

687
46:13.918 --> 46:15.336
that we'd gladly sacrifice.

688
46:17.380 --> 46:19.465
But behind that 90% of sincerity,

689
46:19.591 --> 46:22.302
is the bare truth really so noble and selfless?

690
46:24.846 --> 46:27.223
We give the other person a 90% stake,

691
46:28.558 --> 46:31.603
and maybe protect ourselves with the remaining 10%.

692
46:32.395 --> 46:36.065
But dear Namgung, give me your 100% now,

693
46:36.190 --> 46:37.233
not 10%.

694
46:37.817 --> 46:40.945
All the sorrows you felt because of me, the anger,

695
46:41.696 --> 46:46.159
the frustration, the contempt, give it all back to me, 100%.

696
46:47.076 --> 46:52.206
Whatever it is, if it's from you, I'll gladly take it.

697
46:53.291 --> 46:54.542
I'll accept it all.

698
46:54.667 --> 46:56.169
[shovel scraping]

699
47:03.134 --> 47:04.594
[song swells]

700
47:26.824 --> 47:28.618
[sentimental Korean pop song concludes]

701
47:50.973 --> 47:52.684
Did you two fight?

702
47:54.769 --> 47:56.312
Is that why you came back?

703
47:59.440 --> 48:01.025
He already went through a lot yesterday.

704
48:05.697 --> 48:09.992
No, I meant… We still have work to do.

705
48:10.493 --> 48:14.038
If you let personal issues affect work, then I'm the one who suffers.

706
48:14.163 --> 48:15.498
I see right through you.

707
48:17.458 --> 48:18.501
Don't try so hard.

708
48:24.298 --> 48:25.883
There's nothing between us.

709
48:27.802 --> 48:29.137
[somber music playing]

710
48:30.722 --> 48:32.557
I think you fought because of me.

711
48:33.307 --> 48:35.017
It's just a crush on my side.

712
48:36.018 --> 48:37.812
He doesn't even know I like him.

713
48:41.482 --> 48:42.483
It wasn't because of you.

714
48:43.151 --> 48:44.318
It was my fault.

715
48:47.864 --> 48:49.866
I had feelings for another guy.

716
48:53.745 --> 48:56.873
HAEDAM 1-RI TOWN BUS

717
49:05.173 --> 49:08.092
[Dong-wook] The survival of our company depends on this lawsuit.

718
49:09.010 --> 49:11.679
Ever since Jaekang got involved in the case, I…

719
49:11.804 --> 49:13.473
I don't doubt you, Mr. Han, but…

720
49:14.098 --> 49:16.851
-I need you to understand-- -I understand what you mean.

721
49:16.976 --> 49:18.269
Take me off the case.

722
49:21.814 --> 49:25.193
But you'd be better off with me if you're up against Jaekang.

723
49:25.318 --> 49:27.945
I know exactly what kind of legal strategy they'll use.

724
49:28.070 --> 49:29.405
I can imagine it already.

725
49:30.031 --> 49:30.865
Oh.

726
49:31.491 --> 49:32.950
I won't be on the case anymore.

727
49:34.118 --> 49:35.620
Clients who don't trust me get rejected.

728
49:36.746 --> 49:37.663
[call drops]

729
49:37.789 --> 49:38.956
[sighs]

730
49:39.081 --> 49:40.166
[phone vibrates]

731
49:42.335 --> 49:43.878
HYUNMAN: WITHDRAWING…

732
49:44.003 --> 49:45.922
JEONGSE: CANCELING…

733
49:46.047 --> 49:47.757
BAEKA: DUE TO SOME ISSUES…

734
49:53.095 --> 49:55.681
DELIVERY COMPLETED ORDER: YUKGAEJANG

735
49:56.474 --> 49:57.934
Ah, shit.

736
50:04.732 --> 50:07.151
[quirky music playing]

737
50:31.884 --> 50:33.344
[sneakers squeak]

738
50:33.469 --> 50:34.512
[clears throat]

739
50:39.183 --> 50:40.476
It's been over an hour.

740
50:41.060 --> 50:42.144
It must be cold.

741
50:45.147 --> 50:46.274
You lost weight.

742
50:51.946 --> 50:53.114
Four pounds?

743
50:57.118 --> 50:58.244
[quirky music concludes]

744
51:00.288 --> 51:01.205
[door closes]

745
51:01.330 --> 51:02.832
[Tae-seung] Wait, what are you doing here?

746
51:03.749 --> 51:05.626
Why are you showing up like this after three months?

747
51:07.545 --> 51:09.005
You came to see me too.

748
51:12.466 --> 51:13.843
[light music playing]

749
51:25.104 --> 51:26.480
[moans softly]

750
51:40.536 --> 51:41.621
[sighs]

751
51:47.126 --> 51:48.419
[sighs deeply]

752
52:02.600 --> 52:04.602
[chuckles]

753
52:10.024 --> 52:10.942
[light music concludes]

754
52:11.651 --> 52:12.944
[quirky music playing]

755
52:17.615 --> 52:18.658
[exhales sharply]

756
52:18.783 --> 52:20.368
This is a huge misunderstanding.

757
52:20.660 --> 52:22.036
The reason I went to…

758
52:23.454 --> 52:24.288
Okay.

759
52:26.666 --> 52:28.668
You've been going through a lot, huh?

760
52:31.587 --> 52:33.297
Well, this is all just a big mix-up.

761
52:34.882 --> 52:38.052
The thing is, my trust fund is tied up at the moment, so…

762
52:38.886 --> 52:40.471
this is just temporary.

763
52:41.806 --> 52:42.848
[phone vibrates]

764
52:43.224 --> 52:44.767
There are plenty of clients who want to hire me.

765
52:44.892 --> 52:45.935
It's a long list.

766
52:51.148 --> 52:53.401
[Donglim rep] Attorney Han, we'll have to cancel the retainer.

767
52:53.526 --> 52:54.777
Sorry for the inconvenience.

768
53:01.409 --> 53:02.827
[quirky music concludes]

769
53:05.246 --> 53:06.247
Hey.

770
53:08.207 --> 53:09.959
You came here to watch me fail?

771
53:12.670 --> 53:14.213
Just laugh at me already.

772
53:14.338 --> 53:16.382
"You deserve this for being so arrogant."

773
53:17.133 --> 53:18.300
Didn't you come for that?

774
53:18.676 --> 53:21.137
Do you enjoy belittling yourself like that?

775
53:25.224 --> 53:26.600
You are very young.

776
53:27.601 --> 53:28.894
You can start over.

777
53:29.395 --> 53:30.229
Start over?

778
53:30.896 --> 53:32.064
Sh…

779
53:34.066 --> 53:35.317
How would I even do that?

780
53:37.403 --> 53:38.988
How would a total reset even work?

781
53:39.405 --> 53:42.324
Who would ever hire a lawyer accused of abandoning a trial?

782
53:45.036 --> 53:46.328
Oh, that's right.

783
53:47.163 --> 53:49.415
You're the expert of failure, so enlighten me.

784
53:49.915 --> 53:51.042
What do you think I should do?

785
53:51.542 --> 53:54.045
Be positive, intelligent, and confident?

786
53:54.628 --> 53:55.755
Will that fix it?!

787
53:57.506 --> 53:59.508
[soft music playing]

788
54:04.889 --> 54:07.850
I am the expert of failure, so listen to what I'm about to say.

789
54:09.351 --> 54:12.021
If you trip in the middle of a crowded street,

790
54:12.146 --> 54:16.192
and there's a lot of people staring, do you get up because you're cheerful?

791
54:16.859 --> 54:18.194
Or because you're positive?

792
54:18.319 --> 54:19.278
Oh, no.

793
54:19.403 --> 54:21.030
You get up because you're embarrassed.

794
54:22.948 --> 54:24.492
I didn't get up by staying positive.

795
54:24.617 --> 54:26.118
I got up because I was embarrassed.

796
54:27.453 --> 54:31.290
So if you're embarrassed, just hurry up and get on your feet.

797
54:32.166 --> 54:34.376
Do not waste your time on useless pride.

798
54:46.597 --> 54:47.515
[gasps]

799
55:01.862 --> 55:03.155
[soft music concludes]

800
55:10.538 --> 55:13.541
[washing machine whirring]

801
55:24.718 --> 55:25.845
Tell me what's on your mind.

802
55:27.721 --> 55:31.100
You come here after three months, so you must want to talk.

803
55:35.771 --> 55:36.605
Or not.

804
55:37.148 --> 55:38.107
Just spit it out.

805
55:41.902 --> 55:43.028
Oh, by the way.

806
55:45.156 --> 55:47.116
You knew that I went to go see you.

807
55:48.492 --> 55:50.953
[sighs] You didn't look at me once?

808
55:51.620 --> 55:52.788
That was really cold.

809
55:53.747 --> 55:56.292
Were you playing with my feelings? Did you have fun?

810
55:57.543 --> 55:58.794
[sobs softly]

811
56:01.755 --> 56:02.590
What?

812
56:05.634 --> 56:08.012
Are you crying? Wait, why?

813
56:10.931 --> 56:12.725
I'm the one who should be in tears.

814
56:13.642 --> 56:14.476
Hey, look.

815
56:14.852 --> 56:15.686
Mi-do.

816
56:18.981 --> 56:19.940
Hey, Mi-do.

817
56:26.780 --> 56:28.032
Okay, it's okay.

818
56:28.699 --> 56:30.075
You can play with my feelings.

819
56:30.784 --> 56:31.702
Okay?

820
56:32.536 --> 56:33.370
Go ahead.

821
56:34.079 --> 56:35.122
I said it's okay.

822
56:45.549 --> 56:46.884
Attorney Seo called you, didn't he?

823
56:48.928 --> 56:49.929
Did he threaten you?

824
56:52.097 --> 56:53.057
What did he say?

825
56:53.724 --> 56:54.892
Tell me what he said.

826
56:59.021 --> 56:59.855
It's okay.

827
57:00.731 --> 57:01.899
You can tell me.

828
57:02.691 --> 57:03.567
Hmm?

829
57:12.868 --> 57:13.953
What if…

830
57:17.498 --> 57:18.624
purely hypothetically,

831
57:21.252 --> 57:27.424
I had to choose between you and Namgung and have sex with only one of you?

832
57:29.260 --> 57:33.931
I'd think about it for a whole week, and I would choose you.

833
57:37.268 --> 57:38.310
[tender music playing]

834
57:41.480 --> 57:45.067
But if I had to save only one of you from a terrible fate,

835
57:47.111 --> 57:50.197
I would save my boyfriend without having any second thoughts.

836
57:55.577 --> 57:56.745
[whispers] Wow.

837
57:59.164 --> 58:00.165
Shocking.

838
58:05.921 --> 58:07.339
Do you think I'm that easy?

839
58:08.424 --> 58:09.383
Huh?

840
58:09.717 --> 58:10.676
Am I a joke?

841
58:21.353 --> 58:23.439
But if you're willing to accept that,

842
58:25.232 --> 58:27.151
if it's not important for you,

843
58:30.321 --> 58:31.697
will you go out with me?

844
58:40.831 --> 58:41.832
One month.

845
58:44.293 --> 58:46.462
Do you want to lose your mind with me?

846
58:54.511 --> 58:55.846
[tender music concludes]

847
59:10.903 --> 59:11.737
[Su-a] Hmm.

848
59:11.862 --> 59:13.614
The owner lady got these for us.

849
59:23.374 --> 59:24.708
[sighs]

850
59:26.126 --> 59:29.213
These are the only ice pops I've eaten since I was seven.

851
59:31.006 --> 59:32.341
Except for samples.

852
59:34.218 --> 59:35.052
Hmm.

853
59:35.552 --> 59:37.221
The original flavor is good.

854
59:46.230 --> 59:48.565
My ringtone's been "On the Street" for 20 years.

855
59:51.527 --> 59:55.948
So they think that I'm a fan of Sung Si-kyung.

856
59:58.033 --> 01:00:00.452
But that's the only song of his I know.

857
01:00:04.206 --> 01:00:09.044
In high school, bus 5019 was the only one that went

858
01:00:09.169 --> 01:00:10.629
from my house to school.

859
01:00:11.505 --> 01:00:12.631
In the eleventh grade…

860
01:00:14.675 --> 01:00:20.764
at a bus stop ten minutes further away, they added a new route, bus 8848.

861
01:00:21.807 --> 01:00:23.767
Even though walking ten minutes would get me

862
01:00:23.892 --> 01:00:25.727
to school 20 minutes earlier,

863
01:00:27.396 --> 01:00:29.189
I only took bus 5019.

864
01:00:31.900 --> 01:00:37.239
I thought it was because I was used to it, but now, looking back…

865
01:00:40.367 --> 01:00:41.869
I believe I was scared.

866
01:00:45.706 --> 01:00:47.583
Of taking a path I didn't know.

867
01:00:49.460 --> 01:00:50.961
[thoughtful music playing]

868
01:00:52.254 --> 01:00:53.881
That I could lose my way.

869
01:00:57.217 --> 01:00:59.386
And never be able to come back.

870
01:01:03.807 --> 01:01:06.560
Why are you telling me this story suddenly?

871
01:01:10.647 --> 01:01:11.899
I'm suddenly curious.

872
01:01:15.277 --> 01:01:16.612
Bus 8848.

873
01:01:18.947 --> 01:01:21.200
I don't know where it would have taken me.

874
01:01:22.826 --> 01:01:28.415
If I didn't take the other one, could I still have gone anywhere?

875
01:01:32.044 --> 01:01:33.670
Would it have been okay?

876
01:01:37.925 --> 01:01:39.718
Actually, I'm not really curious.

877
01:01:44.014 --> 01:01:45.849
More like I want to be curious.

878
01:01:50.354 --> 01:01:51.730
So I wonder…

879
01:01:51.855 --> 01:01:53.649
[thoughtful music concludes]

880
01:01:55.526 --> 01:01:57.277
…can I be curious about you?

881
01:02:05.327 --> 01:02:06.745
You can be curious.

882
01:02:10.123 --> 01:02:11.917
Would you date me just for a month?

883
01:02:17.256 --> 01:02:19.049
["Stay" playing]

884
01:02:39.820 --> 01:02:41.697
A LOVE OTHER THAN YOURS

885
01:02:57.129 --> 01:02:58.463
[Mi-do] It's just one month.

886
01:02:58.589 --> 01:03:00.799
[Namgung] Let's try our best with our current partners.

887
01:03:00.924 --> 01:03:02.634
[Su-a] How much touching is allowed?

888
01:03:02.759 --> 01:03:04.094
[Namgung] How much do you want?

889
01:03:04.219 --> 01:03:07.472
[Mi-do] I'll quit for real! I'm never going to do films ever again!

890
01:03:07.598 --> 01:03:08.640
Director Mi-do!

891
01:03:08.765 --> 01:03:10.225
If you decide to date me,

892
01:03:10.601 --> 01:03:12.769
I'll do everything I can to win you over.

893
01:03:12.894 --> 01:03:14.396
How are you? My name is Sol.

894
01:03:14.855 --> 01:03:16.898
[Hwa-young] You are here for Sol's custody, right?

895
01:03:17.149 --> 01:03:21.028
Listen, if it were your father, would you still save Namgung?

896
01:03:27.034 --> 01:03:27.951
[song concludes]
